abstract: >-
  SIGNET encodes directions of bias, links between designs and design validity as
  named linear constraints, decides before results are seen which directional claims
  a body of evidence can certify, and reports certificates, inference that is valid in finite
  samples for known variances, and tolerance to failed assumptions. The code was written by
  generative AI systems (Claude Opus 5.5 and, for version 1.2.0, Claude Fable 5.2; Anthropic) under
  the direction of the author, who is accountable for it; see AI_USE.md.
